==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Dogenstein]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Devil Wife|Devil Wives]] spawn, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
*2 [[Techn-Old Hyena]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 116.67 seconds<sup>3,500f</sup>.
*1 [[Daboo of the Dead]] spawns as the boss after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*4 [[General GreGory|General GreGories]] spawn after 83.33 seconds<sup>2,500f</sup>, delay 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Surprisingly, [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] can do 90% or if boosted even 100% of the meatshield job here, as his [[Immune to Warp|Warp Immune]] [[Talents|Talent]] really shines when it comes to stages with Techn-Old Hyena! Don't worry if you don't have it though, as [[rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] works perfectly here as well!

This is a straight-forward stage: use [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] on Devil Wife to stack up some cash, and start sending out your army, but don't overdo it in case you run out of money. There are hardly any strong pushers here, so stalling and taking your time by chipping Daboo of the Dead should be your main priority. [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] can be one of your primary sources of DPS for every enemy here, but make sure to have [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] prepared to deal the final blow to Daboo, just in case.

It might get a bit overwhelming if the second hyena comes and stacks up with the first, especially with the occasional General GreGories that can stack up with them too, so prepare some well-suitable units for them, all while timing to avoid Daboo's attacks. [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] or/and [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] work against the GreGories, but expect them to get loop-warped/repeatedly staggered after you are done with Gregory. Other general DPS units can be [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] (make sure to send them out sparsely, so as to not drain your income), Talented [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]] and [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]] to take big shots on either Daboo or the Techn-Old Hyena after you are finished with the General GreGories, of which there are 4 in total and appear once every 100 seconds.

If you're having too much trouble dealing with the tag team of Daboo and Techn-Old Hyena, you can slip in talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to nuke the first troublesome Techn-Old Hyena, with proper timing.

